TITLE:: PltView
summary:: Base class for the plots: window, grid, frame, ticks, caption
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PlotLib, Classes/PltScatter

DESCRIPTION::
Everything shared by the plots. Subclass it to add one.

A subclass provides three things:

DEFINITIONLIST::
## strong::dataBounds:: || code::[xLo, xHi, yLo, yHi]:: in data units, or nil for
no grid and no ticks.
## strong::drawData:: || the code::Pen:: calls, placing data with
strong::xPix:: and strong::yPix::.
## strong::caption:: || one line under the plot, or nil.
::

Drawing order is grid, data, frame, ticks, labels, so the frame and the text stay
on top of the data.

code::
PltRamp : PltView {
	var <values;

	*new { |values, title = "ramp"| ^super.new(title, 600, 300).init(values) }
	init { |argValues| values = argValues; this.refresh }

	dataBounds { ^[0, values.size - 1, values.minItem, values.maxItem] }
	caption { ^values.size.asString + "values" }

	drawData { |v, r, b|
		Pen.strokeColor = PlotLib.color(\trace);
		values.do { |y, i|
			var p = Point(this.xPix(i, r, b), this.yPix(y, r, b));
			if(i == 0) { Pen.moveTo(p) } { Pen.lineTo(p) };
		};
		Pen.stroke;
	}
}
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: title
Window title. Defaults to the class name.
argument:: width
argument:: height

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: front
METHOD:: close
Closes the window, which calls strong::free::.

METHOD:: refresh
Redraw, deferred to the AppClock, and a no-op once the window is closed. Safe to
call from a responder or another thread.

METHOD:: free
Release responders, synths and dependants. Called by the window's code::onClose::;
subclasses that hold server resources override it.

METHOD:: writeImage
Write a PNG of the window as it stands, with code::Image.fromWindow::. Call it from
a Routine on the AppClock and wait first: code::drawFunc:: has not run at the moment
code::front:: returns.
code::
Routine({ var p = PltScatter(x, y).front; 0.4.wait; p.writeImage("~/plot.png"); }).play(AppClock);
::

METHOD:: alwaysOnTop
Show the window, keep it above the others, and return the view, so it reads as an
instruction and can end a chain.
code::
m = PltMeter(2, 0).alwaysOnTop;
::

METHOD:: alwaysOnTop_
The same as a setter, so it can be turned off again.
code::
m.alwaysOnTop_(false);
::

METHOD:: isAlwaysOnTop
Whether the flag is set. Qt applies it when the window is shown, so on a window
that has not been fronted yet this reads false until it appears.

METHOD:: position
METHOD:: position_
Where the window sits, the same way link::Classes/ServerMeter:: does it, so a set of
plots can be placed rather than stacked.

note::
Window bounds pass through code::Window.flipY::, so y is measured from the strong::
bottom:: of the screen. Get and set share that convention, so round tripping a
position works, but a y typed by hand may not land where it reads.
::
code::
(
PltMeter(2, 0).position_(20 @ 60).front;
PltSpectrum(0).position_(340 @ 60).front;
)
::

METHOD:: window
METHOD:: view
The Window and the UserView, for anything the class does not cover.

Escape closes the window.

METHOD:: padLeft
METHOD:: padRight
METHOD:: padTop
METHOD:: padBottom
Space around the data area, in pixels. The left pad has to hold the widest y label.

METHOD:: xLabel
METHOD:: yLabel
METHOD:: showTicks
METHOD:: xTicks
METHOD:: yTicks
About how many ticks each axis should get.

METHOD:: plotRect
The data area for a given view, inside the padding.

METHOD:: xPix
METHOD:: yPix
Data units to pixels. y is inverted, so a larger value is higher up.
argument:: x
argument:: r
The plot rect.
argument:: b
The bounds array.

METHOD:: dataBounds
METHOD:: drawData
METHOD:: caption
To override. See the description.

METHOD:: adjustBounds
A last chance to change the visible range once the pixel size is known.
link::Classes/PltScatter:: uses it for equal aspect.

METHOD:: xTickValues
METHOD:: yTickValues
METHOD:: xTickLabel
METHOD:: yTickLabel
Where the ticks go and what they say, in data units. Override these for a
transformed axis and the grid, the labels and the spacing stay in agreement;
link::Classes/PltSpectrum:: does it for logarithmic frequency.

METHOD:: drawPanel
Draw one framed, gridded, ticked box. A stacked view calls it once per panel, with
code::xLabels:: false on all but the lowest.
